            "annotations": [],
            "logprobs": [],
            "text": "{\"strengths\":[\"Clear causal chain from lower confidence to postponed consumption, a fall in aggregate demand, unwanted inventories, and lower real output.\",\"Accurately distinguishes a demand-side contraction from a fall in productive capacity.\",\"Explains conditional outcomes using SRAS responsiveness and possible offsetting changes in other AD components.\"],\"improvements\":[\"Submit the AD–AS diagram referred to in the answer: show AD shifting left from AD1 to AD2, unchanged SRAS, and equilibria showing both Y1→Y2 and P1→P2.\",\"Keep the strong explanation, but ensure every claimed diagram is visible because this task specifically requires the output and price-level effects to be represented diagrammatically.\"],\"mistakes\":[\"Missing required diagram\"],\"examinerComment\":\"Estimated practice mark: 8/10. This is an accurate, focused and well-developed written explanation. It uses relevant terminology, develops the inventory/orders mechanism convincingly, and gives useful conditions affecting the relative size of output and price-level changes. However, the required AD–AS diagram was not submitted, so the diagram described in the prose cannot be credited visually. A correctly labelled diagram would make this a stronger top-band response.\",\"studyNext\":\"Practise drawing a clean AD–AS contraction diagram in under two minutes: Price level and real output axes; SRAS unchanged; AD1 shifting left to AD2; initial and new equilibria; P1/P2 and Y1/Y2 clearly identified.\",\"assessmentFormat\":\"paper_1_a\",\"paper\":\"paper_1\",\"questionPart\":\"a\",\"levelRelevance\":\"shared_sl_hl\",\"assessmentSkills\":[\"diagram_explanation\",\"economic_analysis\"],\"commandTerm\":\"explain\",\"commandTermLabel\":\"Explain\",\"syllabusUnit\":\"unit_3\",\"syllabusTopic\":\"3.2\",\"topicLabel\":\"AD/AS variations\",\"classificationConfidence\":\"high\",\"markingConfidence\":\"high\",\"diagramExpected\":true,\"diagramSubmitted\":false,\"diagramAssessmentStatus\":\"not_submitted\",\"workingsExpected\":false,\"workingsSubmitted\":false,\"workingsAssessmentStatus\":\"not_relevant\",\"attachmentContent\":\"none\",\"assessableEarned\":8,\"markBreakdown\":[{\"label\":\"Knowledge and terminology\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Consumer confidence, consumption, aggregate demand, SRAS and real output are used accurately and appropriately.\"},{\"label\":\"Economic analysis\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The response develops a coherent mechanism from lower confidence through reduced consumption and inventories to lower production, output and the price level, with relevant conditional analysis.\"},{\"label\":\"Diagram\",\"awarded\":0,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The answer describes an appropriate AD–AS diagram, but no image was submitted, so no visual diagram relationship or labels can be assessed.\"},{\"label\":\"Structure and clarity\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The answer is tightly organised, directly answers both requested outcomes, and clearly separates the main mechanism from qualifying conditions.\"}],\"bandRationale\":\"The written response is securely in the 7–8 band because it gives accurate, developed and coherent analysis of both real-output and price-level effects. The absence of the required submitted diagram prevents it from demonstrating the complete diagram-supported response expected for the highest band.\",\"limitations\":[],\"componentEvaluation\":null}"
          }
